# Opinion

Meeting: 0003-improve-the-design-and-aesthetics-of-rps-arena
Agent: Arbiter
Task: Improve the design and aesthetics of RPS Arena
Context:
- Objective: finalize decision on the RPS Arena design refresh scoped to public assets and supporting tests.
- Inputs: architects endorse pure render helpers and lightweight styling; developer implemented sticky nav, hero stats, new CSS tokens, and view utility integration; test engineer confirmed 100% coverage with new uiRender tests and repo pytest run.
- Constraints: no Playwright/screenshots, keep buildless stack, maintain API compatibility.

Position:
- Proceed with the implemented design uplift: it respects constraints, improves UX clarity, and adds sanitization + testability via view helpers.
- No blocking concerns; critic notes to monitor contrast/focus, but current styles retain visible focus outlines.

Recommendations:
- Adopt the new UI as the baseline and keep future visual tweaks within the helper-driven, test-covered pattern.
- Continue running both `npm test` (c8 --100 node --test) and repo-level pytest after UI-affecting changes.
- Keep meeting artifacts updated for subsequent tasks to preserve audit trail.
